00:00:20.614 --> 00:00:27.955
SECRETARY DR. DAVID SHULKIN.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:30.057
&gt;&gt; I WASN'T HAPPY WITH THE SPEED

00:00:28.088 --> 00:00:30.791
WITH WHICH OUR VETERANS WERE

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:34.495
TAKEN CARE OF.

00:00:30.924 --> 00:00:35.362
WE MADE CHANGES BECAUSE WE WANT

00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:36.597
THEM TAKEN CARE OF.

00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:37.331
WE WANT THEM TO HAVE CHOICE.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.299
SO THAT THEY CAN RUN TO A

00:00:37.464 --> 00:00:40.734
PRIVATE DOCTOR.

00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:42.402
&gt;&gt; SHULKIN WASN'T TOO HAPPY

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.104
ABOUT GETTING AXED AND TOOK OUT

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:46.173
HIS FRUSTRATIONS IN A BLISTERING

00:00:44.238 --> 00:00:48.509
OP ED THIS MORNING SAYING

00:00:46.306 --> 00:00:50.377
"WASHINGTON HAS TURNED SO TOXIC,

00:00:48.642 --> 00:00:51.378
CHAOTIC, DISRESPECTFUL AND

00:00:50.511 --> 00:00:52.713
SUBVERSIVE THAT IT BECAME

00:00:51.512 --> 00:00:53.981
IMPOSSIBLE FOR ME TO ACCOMPLISH

00:00:52.846 --> 00:00:55.282
THE IMPORTANT WORK THAT OUR

00:00:54.114 --> 00:00:56.683
VETERANS NEED."

00:00:55.415 --> 00:00:58.719
THE FORMER SECRETARY BLAMED

00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:59.887
CRITICS FOR MAKING FALSE

00:00:58.852 --> 00:01:05.459
ACCUSATIONS AGAINST HIM.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:05.893
THEY SAW ME AS AN OBSTACLE TO

00:01:05.592 --> 00:01:06.960
PRIVATIZATION.

00:01:06.026 --> 00:01:08.162
HIS REMOVAL BOILED OVER

00:01:07.094 --> 00:01:09.730
